WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:06.970
Speaker 1: got a ton of emails from people
saying, David, there is a new straw poll out

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.629
for Republicans in 2024 and Trump isn't winning.

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:13.230
You've got to talk about it.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.730
So I'm going to talk about it.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.430
But for better or worse, I don't know if this
will bring pleasure or disdain or a sadness

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.060
to people in the audience.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.370
It's a pretty meaningless poll.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:28.350
This is a poll from the Western Conservative
Summit.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:35.640
And indeed, Republican Florida Governor Ronda
Santos won over Donald Trump in this straw

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.650
poll that was conducted on Saturday.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.240
Now, let's look at the numbers.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.710
This is a poll in which Ronda Santos came
in first with 74 percent.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.530
Donald Trump was second with 71 percent.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:57.020
Then you have Ted Cruz at 42 percent, Mike
Pompeo at 39 percent, and Tim Scott at 35

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.020
percent.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.820
Now, why is this a meaningless poll result?

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.050
It's meaningless because this is number one.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.620
It's a long time from now, first of all.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.820
Number two, this is an approval poll.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:16.510
So there are two things that make it meaningless
for us for identifying Trump's actual chances

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.010
in 2024.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:25.240
Number one, it just asks you, do you approve
of Trump to Santos, whoever or not?

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.189
Do you support them in 2024 as the Republican
nominee?

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.840
And number two, you can vote yes.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.560
Essentially, I approve for more than one person.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.890
That's why it doesn't add up to 100 percent
to Santa 74, Trump 71.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.590
So this tells us.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:46.770
Very, very little about what's going to go
on in 2024, but I still think that there are

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.909
some interesting things to glean from this.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:52.280
Why is it that DeSantis is doing well?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:58.439
The Santurce is doing well because he is a
more competent and I believe far more dangerous

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:02.479
version of Trump's authoritarian lunacy.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:08.539
In a sense, the Santurce is more Trump being
than Trump to the degree that he can better

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:14.750
communicate his harebrained ideas that he
shares with Donald Trump himself.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:22.130
We've talked before about, you know, could
Donald Trump's presidency open the door to

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:26.920
an even dumber and even more incompetent version
of Trump that Republicans would vote for?

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.000
The answer is absolutely.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.840
As I've said earlier and before, if you overstate
the intelligence of the Republican electorate,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.200
you will be disappointed.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.290
We thought in twenty, fifteen, twenty, sixteen,
OK, there's a lot of ignorant Republicans

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.010
who are easily tricked, but they're not going
to vote for Trump.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.170
They're not this ignorant.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.640
And then they did.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.860
So could they vote for someone even worse
than Trump in terms of cartoonish incompetence?

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:55.959
Yes, but the risk about de Santurce is that
he's more competent than Donald Trump.

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:02.879
He's an authoritarian nut with delusions based
on supply side economic ideas and religious

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:04.780
conservatism and all this stuff.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.200
But he is more competent than Trump.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.250
He is more coherent in the presentation of
these bad ideas, and that has the potential

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:17.580
to make him far more dangerous than Donald
Trump actually is.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.640
And that's a really, really scary thing.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.340
So on the one hand, it's an approval poll.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:29.349
You can say I approve of the Santurce and
I approve of Trump.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:34.630
And so that makes it of limited value to us
right now for twenty twenty four.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.810
It's also approval rather than who would you
vote for.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:41.400
It's also still the first half of twenty twenty
one.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.099
So there are limited things we can glean from
this.

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:52.750
But if I am to glean one thing here, it's
that Donald Trump's worst instincts are present

00:03:52.750 --> 00:04:00.180
in Rhondda Santurce and packaged more competently
in terms of DeSantis, his delivery and quite

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:03.140
frankly, the Santas being from Florida, Florida.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.849
We don't know what the map is going to look
like in 2020 for a lot of it will depend on

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:11.180
how does 2022 go and how much voter suppression
is there in many other things.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:18.759
But there is no doubt that if Florida is important,
the Santurce, as the Republican nominee, could

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:21.699
play a very, very big role there as well.

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:24.199
So don't read too much into this.

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:25.169
But an interesting straw poll nonetheless.

